Improved question: **Which events are instantaneous but gate later timers, and which final-post-roast hand tasks must be serialized because the one cook cannot whisk sauce, dress salad, and plate at the same time?**

Answer: the chicken-pan insertion is the real “chicken goes in” clock anchor; salad starts from that oven event, not from chicken-prep completion; dressing waits 5 minutes from rest start; and the final prep queue must be ordered to avoid one-cook overlap. The earliest complete finish is therefore 84 minutes from program start: 69 minutes of oven-critical work, 8 minutes rest, and then the one-cook tail. I added an inferred zero-duration oven handoff step to expose the “chicken goes in” moment, then revised triggers to wait for that event, for rest + 300 seconds, and for sauce/salad readiness before slicing/plating.

Tracks: `oven` (passive roasting line), `main-prep` (potato/chicken/broccoli hand work), `salad`, `pan-sauce`, and `rest-and-serve`.

